WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:03.048
- How has Orphan Black changed my life.

00:00:03.048 --> 00:00:05.578
How has Orphan Black not changed my life?

00:00:05.578 --> 00:00:08.661
How has Orphan Black changed my life?

00:00:11.895 --> 00:00:13.775
- It's changed my life in
so many different ways,

00:00:13.775 --> 00:00:17.850
not only career wise, just
being able to walk into rooms

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.627
that I would never
normally get to walk into.

00:00:20.627 --> 00:00:23.359
- I had no idea people
were killing off clones.

00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:25.121
I had no idea people were making clones

00:00:25.121 --> 00:00:28.254
and then killing them, and it's not right.

00:00:28.254 --> 00:00:30.714
- It's taught me to dig
down and realize that

00:00:30.714 --> 00:00:32.983
there's goodness in humanity

00:00:32.983 --> 00:00:36.563
and something worth
fighting for in everybody.

00:00:36.563 --> 00:00:39.317
- I just don't think that I
was an actor before the show.

00:00:39.317 --> 00:00:40.238
Like, I know I was an actor.

00:00:40.238 --> 00:00:42.009
Obviously I auditioned

00:00:42.009 --> 00:00:43.842
and I'd worked before,

00:00:45.366 --> 00:00:48.697
but I don't think that I
had fallen in love with

00:00:48.697 --> 00:00:51.693
or been open about how
much I loved acting.

00:00:51.693 --> 00:00:55.004
- Orphan Black was my first on camera job,

00:00:55.004 --> 00:00:58.521
so I've been able to learn for five years

00:00:58.521 --> 00:01:02.380
under the most amazing
mentor I could ever ask for

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.354
in Tatiana.

00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:05.008
- We got to make a show for people

00:01:05.008 --> 00:01:08.761
that didn't have as much
of a voice on television,

00:01:08.761 --> 00:01:10.722
and that means everything to me.

00:01:10.722 --> 00:01:12.969
- Well, I got loads of
free shoes on Friday,

00:01:12.969 --> 00:01:15.779
so I'm sort of good for boots forever.

00:01:15.779 --> 00:01:19.708
- I'm pretty sure that
clones are people too.

00:01:19.708 --> 00:01:22.022
Like, I think technically they're humans,

00:01:22.022 --> 00:01:24.164
so let's stop killing them.

00:01:24.164 --> 00:01:27.343
- Orphan Black has changed my life

00:01:27.343 --> 00:01:30.784
because it has shown me
the power of fiction.

00:01:30.784 --> 00:01:32.863
- When you get people who are real geeks

00:01:32.863 --> 00:01:35.076
and nerds for storytelling and character,

00:01:35.076 --> 00:01:37.417
they actually can change people's lives.

00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:40.396
- If it can push back
the sometimes oppressive

00:01:40.396 --> 00:01:42.185
boundaries of the norm,

00:01:42.185 --> 00:01:45.215
if it can make one person
feel better and prouder

00:01:45.215 --> 00:01:47.208
and more open about their identity,

00:01:47.208 --> 00:01:50.986
then I think fiction has
served its highest purpose.

00:01:50.986 --> 00:01:53.903
- It's unbelievable that this thing

00:01:55.392 --> 00:01:57.684
is now so important to
so many other people.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.957
- The Clone Club has been like

00:01:59.957 --> 00:02:02.813
life-changing in terms of
hearing stories from people

00:02:02.813 --> 00:02:04.380
about how the show's affected them.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.181
- The best supporters,
the most loyal fans,

00:02:06.181 --> 00:02:09.386
and they keep growing and
growing and creating art.

00:02:09.386 --> 00:02:12.452
And it's inspiring to see
their reaction to what we do.

00:02:12.452 --> 00:02:14.750
- I never thought I would work on a show

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:19.033
where people testify that
the show changed their lives,

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:23.493
which is the most astounding
and rewarding thing about it.

00:02:23.493 --> 00:02:27.116
- Giving them a voice, giving
them a conversation starter

00:02:27.116 --> 00:02:29.030
for coming out to their parents.

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:32.068
- We're a show for outsiders

00:02:32.068 --> 00:02:34.018
and for people that were marginalized

00:02:34.018 --> 00:02:35.427
because of who they chose to love

00:02:35.427 --> 00:02:37.007
or who they were attracted to

00:02:37.007 --> 00:02:38.862
or what color they were,

00:02:38.862 --> 00:02:41.307
and we took all of those
characters and outsiders

00:02:41.307 --> 00:02:42.920
and we put them center stage

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.330
and gave them a venue to fight

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.376
and stand up for themselves.

00:02:46.376 --> 00:02:48.938
And I'm very proud of that.

00:02:48.938 --> 00:02:52.188
- How has Orphan Black changed my life?

00:02:55.361 --> 00:02:57.361
I made lifelong friends.

00:02:59.304 --> 00:03:00.137
Yeah.

00:03:02.948 --> 00:03:05.448
- [Cast] Thank you Clone Club.

